<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title><%= lab.name %> — PingOne Labs</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials/header') %>
  <main class="container">
    <%- include('partials/lab-content') %>

    <% if (configured) { %>
    <section class="panel device-flow-panel">
      <h2>Smart TV Simulator</h2>
      <p class="hint device-flow-intro">
        This simulates an input-constrained device (smart TV, set-top box, or IoT display).
        The TV requests a <strong>device code</strong> and shows a <strong>user code</strong> for you to enter on a phone or laptop — the classic RFC 8628 Device Authorization Grant.
      </p>

      <div id="device-flow-app" class="device-flow-layout"
        data-client-id="<%= clientId %>"
        data-issuer="<%= issuer %>">

        <div class="tv-shell">
          <div class="tv-bezel">
            <div class="tv-brand">PingOne Stream</div>
            <div id="tv-screen" class="tv-screen" data-screen="welcome">
              <div class="tv-screen-inner">
                <div class="tv-icon" aria-hidden="true">📺</div>
                <p id="tv-status-line" class="tv-status-line">Press OK on your remote to sign in</p>

                <div class="tv-code-block">
                  <p class="tv-code-label">Enter this code at</p>
                  <a id="tv-verification-uri" class="tv-verification-uri" href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener"></a>
                  <p id="tv-user-code" class="tv-user-code">— — — —</p>
                </div>

                <p id="tv-countdown" class="tv-countdown"></p>
                <p id="tv-poll-status" class="tv-poll-status"></p>
                <div id="tv-error" class="tv-error hidden"></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="tv-remote-hint">
              <button id="tv-start" type="button" class="tv-remote-btn" title="Simulate remote OK">OK</button>
              <button id="tv-reset" type="button" class="tv-remote-btn secondary hidden" title="Reset TV">Reset</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="hint tv-footnote">The TV has no keyboard — authorization happens on your secondary device.</p>
        </div>

        <aside class="device-flow-inspector-panel">
          <h3>OAuth Configuration</h3>
          <p class="hint">Live values from this device authorization session.</p>
          <dl id="oauth-inspector" class="oauth-inspector"></dl>

          <h3>Token Endpoint Polling</h3>
          <p class="hint">The TV polls with <code>grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code</code> until PingOne returns tokens or the code expires.</p>
          <div id="poll-log" class="poll-log"></div>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <div class="device-flow-results hidden">
        <h3>Tokens received on the TV</h3>
        <h4>Token summary (JWT headers decoded)</h4>
        <pre id="device-token-output"></pre>
        <h4>Userinfo</h4>
        <pre id="device-user-output"></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="panel">
      <h2>How the two devices interact</h2>
      <ol class="setup-steps device-flow-steps">
        <li><strong>TV (this simulator)</strong> — POSTs to PingOne <code>device_authorization_endpoint</code> and receives <code>device_code</code> + <code>user_code</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Your phone / laptop</strong> — Open the verification URI, sign in, and enter the user code shown on the TV.</li>
        <li><strong>TV polls</strong> — Repeatedly POSTs to the token endpoint with the <code>device_code</code> until authorization completes (<code>authorization_pending</code> until approved).</li>
        <li><strong>Tokens on TV</strong> — Access token (and ID token) are returned to the constrained device — no redirect URI or browser on the TV required.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <% } %>
  </main>
  <script src="/device-flow/tv-simulator.js"></script>
  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
